MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "City of Evil, Curse and The Crusade fit because I want heavy riffs and energetic guitar work with memorable melodies, which connect with my In Flames and Advance And Vanquish listening.",
    "One-X fits the heavy, emotional hard rock I enjoy in One Day Remains and Ten Thousand Fists, while Healthy In Paranoid Times gives me a reason to explore more from Our Lady Peace after Elocation."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Beautiful Letdown feels too light for what I want now; my interest in some alternative rock does not mean I am currently looking for a softer sound.",
    "Inhuman Rampage and Unhallowed connect with parts of my taste, but speed or greater heaviness alone would not make me choose them today. I am more drawn to groove, darker moods and strong hooks."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat an interest in heavy music as equal enthusiasm for speed, aggression and extreme vocals, although those qualities serve different moods for me.",
    "Some choices stretch my rock listening too broadly: the aggression of Infest or the punk direction of Sing The Sorrow is not enough to make either a priority right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choices, Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days, make darker atmosphere and rhythmic weight especially relevant to what I want next.",
    "I care about how melody and heaviness work together. A recommendation becomes more compelling when its hooks and emotional tone appeal alongside its guitar work."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in melodic heavy music, but sometimes treated nearby styles as equally appealing without capturing my current preference for groove, dark moods and strong hooks."
}
